title: Dashboard › Arrive › What the page shows
route: /dashboard
intro: Four ways to land on the Dashboard, how filters in the address are read, and the parts of the page from the top down: one daily work list. Each part continues in its own diagram.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Click 'Dashboard' in the sidebar\nThe badge counts Info requested"
start s2 "Open the app at /\nThe address / goes to /dashboard"
start s3 "Follow a link with a request or a filter\nA notification, or a button on another page"
start s4 "Demo menu › Click 'Reset demo data'"
toast t1 "'Demo data reset'\n'Everything is back to the starting point.'"

process p1 "Page opens and reads the address"
decision d1 "Does the address hold payer, program, type or stage?"
process p2 "The address wins\nFour menus go back to All, then the address values apply\nUnknown values are ignored"
process p3 "The remembered filters are written back to the address\nFirst visit: no filters"
store w1 "Filters\nPayer, Program, Request type, Stage"

screen sc "Dashboard\nOne daily work list; the filters decide what it shows"
decision d2 "Does the address hold ?request=ID?"
decision d3 "Is there a request with that ID?"
overlay o1 "Request drawer opens over the page"
process p4 "Nothing opens\nThe ?request part is removed after 0.2 seconds"
end e1 "Page shown with no drawer"

group gPage "On the page, from the top down"
  screen h1 "Headline and sub line\n'18 requests are waiting on payers. 3 are waiting on you.'"
  click ca "Click 'Check all now'\nDisabled while Navigator is paused in Settings"
  screen fs "Summary from FLO\n'From today's demo data'\nThree short lines, each with a link: who needs you and what is due soonest, authorizations that end this week, denial deadlines this week"
  screen kf "Four key figures\nNeeds you 3, Due within 24 hours 12, Waiting on payers 18, Denials to act on 8\nEach is a button that applies its filter"
  screen f1 "Filter bar\n'All payers', 'All programs', 'All request types', 'All stages'"
  screen rq "Requests, one table\n'Waiting on you first, then the nearest clock.'\n'Showing 8 of 40', six columns, four sortable headings, 'Show 8 more'"
endgroup

goto g1 "Continues in: Dashboard › Request drawer › Open and read a request"
goto g2 "Continues in: Dashboard › Headline › What the headline and sub line say"
goto g3 "Continues in: Dashboard › Header › Check all now and the demo clock"
goto g4 "Continues in: Dashboard › Filters › Payer, Program, Request type and Stage"
goto g5 "Continues in: Dashboard › Key figures › Click a figure to filter the list"
goto g10 "Continues in: Dashboard › Summary from FLO › What the three lines say and where they lead"
goto g6 "Continues in: Dashboard › Requests table › Order, rows and paging"
goto g9 "Continues in: Dashboard › Filters › Clear filters and empty states"

s1 --> p1
s2 --> p1
s3 --> p1
s4 --> t1 --> p1
p1 --> d1
d1 -->|Yes| p2 --> w1
d1 -->|No| p3 --> w1
w1 --> sc
sc --> d2
d2 -->|No| e1
d2 -->|Yes| d3
d3 -->|Yes| o1 --> g1
d3 -->|No| p4 --> e1

sc --> h1 --> fs --> kf --> f1 --> rq
h1 --> g2
h1 --> ca --> g3
fs --> g10
f1 --> g4
f1 --> g9
kf --> g5
rq --> g6
